    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-18T21:18:04+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-18T21:18:04+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T10:48:04Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-18T10:48:04Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system and associated trough over Western Australia move over western South Australia this evening and broadly across the state during Thursday, clearing to the east early Friday. A high pressure system will then move across southern SA from Friday, before a trough and cold front move across the west late Saturday and across the rest of SA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-18T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with destructive winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding west of Coober Pedy. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers east of Coober Pedy, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding. Winds north to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h increasing to 35 km/h before turning west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon and evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 36.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">The chance of a thunderstorm east of Stuart Highway in the early morning. Sunny day. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the morning then tending southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 37.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h during the morning then tending north to northwesterly 30 to 45 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching around 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Woomera in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Woomera in the morning. Winds northwest to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the morning then tending southerly 25 to 35 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to 20 to 28 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
